WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:12.269
Estonia might be a country that you’ve only
hear about on the Eurovision Song Contest...

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:14.870
If you are one of the few people who actually
watch that.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:20.410
But the reality is Estonia is a pioneering
country in many fields, some might even call

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.859
it the Silicon Valley of Europe.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:26.480
Companies like Skype and TransferWise were
both created here.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.410
This is surprising given that just 30 years
ago, this country was part of the Soviet Union.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.790
In fact, geographically Estonia’s situation
is far from ideal.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:42.140
Their weather there is pretty terrible and
they have fewer than three hours of daylight

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.920
in some winter months.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.730
Plus, they have a never-ending demographic
crisis that seems almost impossible to resolve.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.140
Unlike most countries, the female population
of Estonia is significantly higher than the

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.280
male population.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.180
This means, people find it harder to find
a partner and have children.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:03.830
This is why every year Estonia maintains a
course of population reduction.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.729
And yet, despite all of this, Estonia is still
the most technologically modern country in

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:09.930
all of Europe.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:15.399
In fact, it is the only nation where the access
to internet is recognized in the Constitution.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:21.039
But what makes Estonia get into our Countries
Hall of Fame is the so-called E-RESIDENCY.

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:28.369
This means: any person, no matter where are
they from, can fill a form and become a virtual

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:32.479
citizen of the country.

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:34.100
But what does this really mean?

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.659
Today, we are going to explain you this, but
before we get into that, let´s look back

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:40.509
at their history.

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:44.700
TITLE: THE FIRST VICTIMS OF VLADIMIR PUTIN

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.689
In 1991, Estonia got its independence from
the Soviet Union.

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:53.579
Yes, other countries like Belarus or Ukraine
did at the same time.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:59.530
But in those cases, their new democratically
elected governments had a strong influence

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.880
from the former communist elite.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.850
Estonia was different.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:08.429
Their first democratic Prime Minister, Mart
Laar, formed a cabinet with an average age

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:10.619
of 30 years old.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:15.420
These where young people with new ideas and
who had no debts with the Soviet old guard.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.250
This is how Estonia opened their economy to
the international market.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:23.750
They adopted a capitalist system and a fairly
unique political system that would become

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.189
well known for its minimalism.

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:31.170
Actually, this is the word that defines Estonia
better than any other: MINIMALISM.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:36.819
Even their flag is a simplistic representation
of their traditional landscape.

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:42.660
Even their taxation follows a so-called “flat
rate tax system.”

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.660
What does this mean?

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:48.540
Well, here everyone pays the same percentage
of tax, no matter how much do they earn.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.459
In this case, their income tax is just 20%.

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:56.150
With these policies, it´s easy to understand
why they quickly attracted foreign investments,

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.690
especially from Finland and other Scandinavian
countries.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.930
Nonetheless, this was not enough to grow at
the rate they wanted.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.959
At the beginning of the 90s, just half of
the population had phones in their homes.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.239
Further the infrastructure, built during the
Soviet era, were far from acceptable.

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:17.910
And as you can imagine, this is not a great
set up for a country wanting economic recovery.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.510
Since they had no money to build physical
roads, they decided to invest what they had

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.280
in virtual roads: the country's telecommunications.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:32.599
And, 15 years later, Estonia was the first
country on Earth to implement an electronic

00:03:32.599 --> 00:03:33.790
voting system.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.720
But hold on a second because all these reforms
didn´t come for free.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.980
During these 15 years of forward progress,
the Russian minority that used to rule over

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.849
Estonia became politically isolated.

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:53.329
This is why in 2007, the Kremlin, with Putin
in office, decided to act.

00:03:53.329 --> 00:03:56.750
This is how the first cyber attack in history
was organized.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:01.140
And yes, a cyber attack on a government that
relied heavily on a digital infrastructure

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.099
became a big deal.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:08.819
During the attack, Estonia lost their administration
- which meant even the hospitals couldn’t

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:09.819
function.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:13.420
This is why, since that day, NATO has based
their cyber-security headquarters in Tallinn,

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.579
the Estonian capital.

00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:18.730
But that was not the end of Estonia’s problems…

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.980
TITLE: THE FINANCIAL CRISIS

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:27.949
Two years later, in 2009, the financial crisis
struck the Estonian economy hard, which was

00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:30.600
especially exposed because of it’s significant
foreign investment.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.280
All of a sudden, the government had no money.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.650
Plus, this was the time when they were supposed
to adopt the Euro as their currency.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:43.520
So, even if they wanted to switch, they didn’t
have the money to set up a new currency in

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.520
the country.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:53.390
So they had two options: cut spending or raise
taxes dramatically.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.850
Unlike other countries like Spain, Estonia
took the first option.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:02.840
In a matter of months the Government fired
over 10,000 workers, which was a third of

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.260
their entire staff.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:08.740
Politicians lowered their salaries and froze
all state investments, including many construction

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.740
projects.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:15.660
All of these budget cuts caused the Estonian
GDP to fall 14% that year.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:21.669
To make a comparison, the US, at their worst
moment, saw their GDP fall just 8%.

00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:32.310
Nonetheless, after going through a terrible
2009, Estonia started to recover immediately.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:36.100
Since they didn’t raise taxes and their
business policies were quite flexible, many

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.180
of those who lost their jobs started their
own companies.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:42.160
Now, let´s take a look at their unemployment
chart…

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:48.919
Between 2008 and 2009, Estonia went from a
4% unemployment rate to a 19% rate.

00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:55.100
At the time, this was the highest rate in
all of Europe, even bigger than Spain or Greece.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.930
However, in just two years, they cut this
figure in half.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:02.660
And now, they have a admirable 6%.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.090
The same goes for their salaries.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:10.090
Today, a person who works in Tallinn is making
more money than most people in Southern Europe.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.610
In summary: Estonia is a model for other countries
to follow.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.800
And now we’re going to have a look to see
what they key aspects were that made this

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:20.260
country quite so successful.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:23.360
TITLE: DIGITAL ADMINISTRATION

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.370
Estonia pioneered the creation of the “digital
ID card.”

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.889
Now many other countries are copying this
model… but it’s never been quite as successful

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:33.210
as the original.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:38.520
The reason is that the ID card is actually
useful.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:44.229
For instance, during the elections, any citizen
can take this card, connect it to a computer

00:06:44.229 --> 00:06:47.139
and vote no matter where they are.

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:49.500
There is no need for registration.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:57.669
This is particularly convenient if you are
on holiday or if you live in another country.

00:06:57.669 --> 00:07:02.990
Every expat knows the hassle of voting while
abroad - waiting at the embassy to cast a

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.990
ballot.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:10.210
Further, there have been many elections where
the votes coming in from abroad get lost…

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:15.560
In Estonia you can use your ID card to do
any kind of paperwork with the government…

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.680
including paying taxes.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:23.500
And forget about those long forms that other
tax authorities insist you fill out.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.850
In Estonia, you can everything using your
mobile phone in a matter of minutes.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:32.710
In fact the government has access to the banks,
so they can easily find out your income.

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.610
This happens in every other country, including
the US.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:39.840
The only difference is that in Estonia, they
think it’s stupid to ask the same question

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:40.840
twice.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:50.300
So you simply go over your citizen profile,
confirm all the data, and pay in one click.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.889
But hold on a minute because the best is yet
to come...

00:07:53.889 --> 00:07:58.300
Imagine that one government official wants
to spy on personal data.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:02.610
Well, then you will get a notification on
the control panel of your government profile.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.740
You can even see, exactly who the person is
who is looking at your information and even

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:11.620
request an explanation on why is he or she
doing that.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:18.970
This means, Estonia has way more transparency
and privacy controls than any other democracy.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:22.949
But if you still think this is not enough,
here it comes the thing that puts Estonia

00:08:22.949 --> 00:08:27.379
over the top...

00:08:27.379 --> 00:08:28.379
TITLE: ESTONIAN E-RESIDENCY

00:08:28.379 --> 00:08:33.060
We have all heard about big companies that
place their fiscal headquarters in Panama

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.159
or Luxembourg.

00:08:34.159 --> 00:08:46.150
However, this kind of tax structure is almost
impossible for an SME or a freelancer.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:55.230
Well, in Estonia they realized that they needed
new citizens.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:59.310
As I said, the country faces a demographic
crisis and their weather sucks.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:04.360
This is why in 2014 they decided to offer
their cutting-edge administration to the whole

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.650
world, no matter where a person comes from.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.990
And now you might wonder: why is this useful?

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:17.550
Of course, this is not the equivalent to a
citizenship visa and you can’t use it as

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:18.700
a passport.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:23.890
But it is a digital identity issued by an
European Government, and it helps if you want

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:27.220
to make international transactions or open
a bank account in Estonia.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:32.000
Something that might be useful if you are
watching this video from a place like Ukraine

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.000
or Venezuela.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:38.089
This virtual card also makes it even easier
for you to start a company in Estonia without

00:09:38.089 --> 00:09:41.010
moving there or doing a lot of complex paper
work.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:46.190
OK, now I can hear you now saying…

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:48.250
Estonia is a fiscal haven, right?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.180
Well, sorry, but no...

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:54.060
Corporate tax in Estonia is about 20%, which
is the same as they pay in Finland for example.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:59.650
What Estonia offers are two things: rule of
law and simplicity.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.490
Maybe you think that’s too little to offer?

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:05.850
But, they have already had over 10,000 people
register - in just two years.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:11.029
Among them, there is the Japanese Prime Minister,
Shinzo Abe.

00:10:11.029 --> 00:10:17.880
In other words, Estonia has invented a brand
new concept: the “liquid citizenship.”

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:28.160
And now here is our question for you: Do you
think other countries will follow this model?

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.079
There will be a time where everyone chooses
Estonia citizenship?

00:10:32.079 --> 00:10:34.680
